{{--
  The development toolbar's stats bar (`#start/dev_toolbar`).

  In its own partial, and included with `@includeIf` rather than wrapped in
  an `@if`, because `@serverStats()` is registered by a package that is not
  installed in production. Edge resolves tags when it *compiles* a template;
  a partial is only compiled if it is actually included, so this file is
  never parsed in an environment where the tag does not exist. Inside an
  `@if` in the layout it would be parsed either way.

  The tag inlines its own CSS and JS — no asset to build, and nothing added
  to the Vite entrypoints. That inline script is also why
  `#config/shield` relaxes `script-src` when this is switched on.
--}}
@serverStats()
